      },
      "overlays": {
        "pin": {
          "label": "Tuskegee",
          "sub": "Alabama"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "carver",
      "text": "There, he hired a young scientist named George Washington Carver.",
      "visual": {
        "kind": "card",
        "image": "carver",
        "crop": [
          0.05,
          0.0,
          0.95,
          0.7
        ],
        "caption": "George Washington Carver"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "invite",
      "text": "On October 16, 1901, just weeks into his presidency, Theodore Roosevelt invited him to dinner at the White House.",
      "visual": {
        "kind": "photo",
        "image": "tr",
        "focus": [
          0.48,
          0.3
        ],
        "zoom": [
          1.1,
          1.18
        ],
        "anchor": [
          0.45,
          0.3
        ]
      },
      "overlays": {
        "stamp": "Oct. 16, 1901"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "family",
      "text": "That evening, he sat down to eat with the President and his family.",
      "visual": {
        "kind": "photo",
        "image": "face",
        "focus": [
          0.56,
          0.36
        ],
        "zoom": [
          1.0,
          1.06
        ],
        "anchor": [
          0.46,
          0.36
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "fury",
      "text": "Southern newspapers erupted. The Atlanta Constitution called it an insult. The Memphis Scimitar called it an outrage.",
      "section": "cost",
      "visual": {
        "kind": "title",
        "title": "Outrage",
        "sub": "in Southern newspapers"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "retreat",
      "text": "Roosevelt kept asking Washington for advice. But he never invited him to dine again.",
      "visual": {
        "kind": "photo",
        "image": "tr",
        "focus": [
          0.48,
          0.32
        ],
        "zoom": [
          1.0,
          1.06
        ],
        "anchor": [
          0.45,
          0.34
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "legacy",
      "text": "One meal. And it showed how far America still had to go.",
      "section": "legacy",
      "visual": {
